    "intro_html":  "Order a turkey Reuben at a deli and you get turkey, sauerkraut, Swiss, and Russian dressing on grilled rye. Order fourteen of them and you get a bill you do not want to look at. This bakes the whole sandwich into a pan instead: buttered rye cubes on the bottom, turkey and kraut and Swiss layered through, dressing whisked in. Each serving lands at {{cal}} calories with \u003cstrong\u003e{{protein}} grams of protein\u003c/strong\u003e for about \u003cstrong\u003e${{cost_ps}}\u003c/strong\u003e (at everyday cost).",
